/-
Johnson/Desc/First/Att/K05LawOne.lean: KIND K5's LAW IN ONE STATEMENT, AT ITS WIDEST FORM, ITS
PREMISES AS THREE RECORDS: what is a test on public data (K5Public), what is asked at each statement
in front with "on" (K5AtOn), and what is asked of the relation behind the kind (K5Behind).

THE STATEMENT. The piece ⟨{ attentionKind seatSO claims p with planOk := ok }, base, ds, [], the identity,
Err.cap kc⟩ (the kind's block at the hearing's seat, whatever its test on the plan, its runs and its
type of claims; any plain stretch of written rounds with the kind's entries; at each round the error
‹the round's challenges› / 2 ^ kc) is good (Piece.GoodIn, Johnson/Desc/Sound/GoodIn.lean): from
"on"; to LaidBehind and a promise that has ridden; from the chain's first joint's Todo at the
lookup's typed out-statement and the world's part that an item pins; to the relation behind.

Main names:
  `Rides Fr base`: a promise that rides: a reading rq of the record with ReadsRest
    (Att/K05SeatKeeps.lean) and a q that is carried along SameBelow (Att/K05SeamOut.lean).
  `K5Public`: THIRTEEN fields, each a test on public data. `K5AtOn`: THREE, each "∀ a, on a → …".
    `K5Behind`: TWO, BOTH ASKED ONLY WHERE LaidBehind HOLDS: the forms' worth (BillsWorthJ,
    Att/K05BillsWorth.lean) at the record that the claims' seat itself hands in for the lookup's
    three tables (lookOfO, Att/LookO.lean), and the item.
  THE JOINTS: `own_recOf` (the place's record is recOf of the closed parameters) · `hK_of_left`
    (what the bill's payment of the returns asks of the lookup's heard record, from K3LeftOutIs) ·
    `hlk_of_left` (the seat's record has the heard point, and its test on the planes is a public
    one) · `sized_of_laid` (**the ledger behind the hearing is Sized**, drawn from LaidBehind and
    K3LeftOutIs).
  `K05_law_one`: **the one theorem.** `K05_law_one_means`: with OwnMeans (Att/K05Means.lean) in
    front.
  `PinItemP.atSeatSO`: an item whose law "lay" is paid by ReadsRest. `K05_yes_fails_cap`: the text
    that says yes to all is NOT good at the cap, wherever the policy's work is below kc (under a
    pair (a, w) that is a premise): so the form can fail.

LETTERS THAT HAVE FALLEN against Att/K05PinP.lean's widest form: nx (it is x.F.next: K3LeftOutIs and
Room force it) · k (0: the weakest promise) · m0 (the zero tuple) · j0 (chosen: there is a listed
name wherever there is a pair) · the plan record of the dry run (A with its number of calls laid) ·
the record for the lookup's tables (the seat's own). yOf stays, idle.
WHAT STANDS BESIDE THE LAW AND IS NO FIELD. (1) The guards of the caller's reading (the lookups'
AttReadsOK) and "the committed symbols are the packing of small integers": without them a
symbol, a mask entry or a cell without a seat, and every cell of a column that is no packing, is
read as 0 in silence: the law is true of that reading. (2) WHAT THE ITEM PINS IS NOT SAID: I is a
letter: holds := False, ok := False, a constant part meet its laws. (3) k5Held is asked at p's own
work. (4) Err.cap counts a round's challenges with the bits of work: no sentence on bits follows
from this file. (5) ns (the ledger's number of mask entries: Room.ns) and x.ns (in the type of the
caller's entries) are two letters: the proof asks no tie: the kind's own slots are read through
attLin's maskOf, at any number. (6) The dry run's letters iU3, nW, Kc, k3, nzx, tj are free: whoever
fills them says whence (Att/K05PublicB.lean fills all but tj from the block's own test on the plan).
(7) pl (the lookup's plain cells ↦ the caller's entries) stands in K5AtOn.left alone and is fenced
by nothing here: a constant meets the law: its truth is the lookup's row's: ONE pl for both rows. α
stands in attLin: in the relation in front and in worth alike: never fenced. (8) Whence the place x:
a letter; at a public record X the lookups' lookAt X i false (Look/LookAt.lean) makes one.
(9) TWO TESTS BEAR ONE NAME: K5Public.planes is Look.planesOk x.fs lmb; AttOK.planes is
(Forest.planeCols x.fs x.lm).toBool. (10) worth speaks of the world of the ledger BEHIND THE
HEARING, and the join's run is taken at that ledger and the tape tj: whoever pays worth from a later
ledger owes that the forms' worth does not turn on the way: not looked at here.
(11) THE LAW HAS NO OBJECT IN THIS FILE: it is a rule over letters. The blocks that it is meant for
are the constants k5AtU and k5AtO: see (12). Whether a description in this library names either is
not said here; the set of lots that has run seats, in a harness file, a text of its own
that is k5AtU's token for token, by reading.
(12) No theorem of this file sets the law at these two constants
(Johnson/Desc/First/Att/SeatU.lean [not in this library],
Johnson/Desc/First/Att/SeatO.lean), which are made at the plan of a public record: the field
K5Public.plan asks a return of Attention.plan. The plan in a record that Verify.publicOf returns is
such a return but for the field seam.tl.plFor (Fo.PubA.public_A_plFor,
OnBytes/Tie/Pv/Lookup/Ends/FoPublicAPlFor.lean). Where the policy has attention segments publicOf
lays an owner into that field: the number of the sub-proof that owns the array which the attention
sub-proof reads of another (HTailF2.borderMeans, OnBytes/Model/Tail.lean). borderMeans refuses where
an owner stands already and lays one where none stands: so the plan that the planner returned bore
none, and the stored plan bears one: they are two plans. By reading, and by an evaluation at the
library's two written policies, no return of Attention.plan bears an owner there. None of these
sentences on an owner is a theorem. So, on that reading, K5Public.plan is not to be had of the
stored plan. K05_law_one and K05_law_one_means name no public record.
EMPTY AT: on := False · R' := False · kc := 0. NONE OF THE
THREE RECORDS IS SHOWN OF ANYTHING HERE. NO MEMBER OF THE WHOLE IS SHOWN. The block is bare: neither
guarded, nor narrowed, nor lifted over a public part.
No soundness of the protocol is claimed: the premises named are not shown.
Nothing is claimed on completeness or hiding.

-/
